</tbody></table>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 36pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 36pt; text-align: justify;">For the <em style="font: inherit;">three</em> and <em style="font: inherit;">nine</em> months ended <em style="font: inherit;"> August 31, 2026</em>, the Company recorded a net loss and, as such, diluted loss per share is the same as basic loss per share, as the inclusion of any potentially dilutive securities would be antidilutive. Stock options, RSUs, and PSUs that could potentially dilute basic earnings per share ("EPS") in the future were excluded from the computation of diluted loss per share because their effect would be antidilutive. RSUs excluded from the computation of diluted loss per share for the <em style="font: inherit;">three</em> and <em style="font: inherit;">nine</em> months ended <em style="font: inherit;"> August 31, 2026</em> include <ix:nonFraction id="c151654114" contextRef="d_2026-06-01_2026-08-31_AntidilutiveSecuritiesExcludedFromComputationOfEarningsPerShareByAntidilutiveSecuritiesAxis-RestrictedStockUnitsRsusPerformancebasedMember" unitRef="Share" name="us-gaap:AntidilutiveSecuritiesExcludedFromComputationOfEarningsPerShareAmount" scale="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="INF">92,935</ix:nonFraction> PSUs subject to performance conditions and <ix:nonFraction id="c151654115" contextRef="d_2026-06-01_2026-08-31_AntidilutiveSecuritiesExcludedFromComputationOfEarningsPerShareByAntidilutiveSecuritiesAxis-RestrictedStockUnitsRSUsMarketbasedMember" unitRef="Share" name="us-gaap:AntidilutiveSecuritiesExcludedFromComputationOfEarningsPerShareAmount" scale="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="INF">19,395</ix:nonFraction> PSUs subject to market conditions, which are contingently issuable upon the satisfaction of conditions that had <em style="font: inherit;">not</em> been satisfied as of <em style="font: inherit;"> August 31, 2026. </em>For the <em style="font: inherit;">three</em> and <em style="font: inherit;">nine</em> months ended <em style="font: inherit;"> August 31, 2025</em>, the Company recorded net income and, as such, used diluted weighted-average common shares outstanding when calculating diluted income per share for the <em style="font: inherit;">three</em> and <em style="font: inherit;">nine</em> months ended <em style="font: inherit;"> August 31, 2025</em>. Stock options and RSUs that could potentially dilute basic earnings per share (&#8220;EPS&#8221;) in the future are included in the computation of diluted income per share.</p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 36pt; text-align: justify;">&#160;</p>
